.TH CLRU_INIT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
clru_init \- initialise a previously declared LRU cache variable
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <clrucache.h>

clru_init(name, capacity, getter, setter, evict_cb);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Calls clrucache_create_full() with the key and value types inferred from
the companion variables created by clru_declare(), and assigns the result
to name. Calls fatal_err() if creation fails.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name       Cache variable (must have been declared with clru_declare
           or clru_declare_scoped)
capacity   Maximum number of live entries before eviction
getter     Remote getter callback, or NULL
setter     Remote setter callback, or NULL
evict_cb   Eviction callback, or NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Calls fatal_err() on allocation failure.
Use clrucache_create_full() directly if you need to handle errors
gracefully.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
clru_declare(cache, int, double);
clru_init(cache, 64, NULL, NULL, NULL);
clru_destroy(cache);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clru_declare (3),
.BR clru_construct (3),
.BR clrucache_create_full (3)
